laurel 3050: LAUREL WDOG: the stuck-CPU report says whether the silent core's clock runs, and tries a SEV; the bark's "pet thread last ran" is read after the reports. Both kernels. docs/laurel_sprout/watchdog.md section 16.

[V 2026-11-03..07, 26 catches] One core per cluster stops dead under full load, always the same core (silver cpu 5 in 8-CPU boots,
gold cpu 1 in 4-CPU boots), in EL0 (modelmanagerd, iconservicesagent, audiomxd, runningboardd: objc_msgSend, swift_allocBox) and
inside system calls (madvise, mmap, kevent_id, getdirentries64), its timer PPI and the SGI pending at the redistributor, nothing active,
no handler running, its trap count frozen. Nothing in the code masks interrupts at EL0 (the emulator writes NZCV only, every EL0 return
takes the saved SPSR), the only SPI this port enables is the bark, GICR_ISACTIVER0 is 0: the GIC CPU interface is not wedged. What is
left: the core executes nothing (a stall on the bus, a trap into a world above EL1: the EL2 vectors of start.s are `b .`, or TrustZone),
or its clock is stopped. The report could not tell these apart. Now, in the same lines, with reads only:
- "core state: OSM cycles in 10 ms: N (M MHz)": the OSM's per-core cycle counter (clk-cpu-osm.c OSM_CYCLE_COUNTER_STATUS_REG 0x9c0 +
  4 * core), read twice 10 ms apart from the reporting CPU, next to the same count of a core of the same cluster that answers (the
  reference proves the register counts at all). 0: the clock is stopped (WFI/WFE with no wake, or off). Near the cluster's MHz: it runs.
- GICR_WAKER of the silent core: ProcessorSleep set would mean the redistributor forwards nothing.
- At the first line of a silence (2 s) one SEV: a core parked in WFE with its interrupt masked wakes on it; nothing else notices a SEV.
- The bark's "pet thread last ran 960767920505705 ms ago" [V 05:19:53, 05:21:55, 05:24:16]: `now` was read before the eight reports
  (seconds of kprintf) and the pet thread stamped a later time on another CPU: the difference wrapped. Read again after the reports;
  a stamp after now prints 0.
New export in bsd/dev/laurel_thermal.c: laurel_osm_core_cycles(mpidr, &cycles), false before the tables are mapped.

